1.Aim

Write a program to load,clean and exploring the data using python.

2.Algorithm

1.Start the program.
2.Import Pandas and NumPy libraries.
3.Create a dataset containing Team, Runs and Wickets.
4.Convert the dataset into a DataFrame.
5.Display the original data.
6.Check for missing values.
7.Replace missing values with the mean.
8.Display the cleaned data.
9.Display the first five rows.
10.Display information and statistical summary.
11.Display the shape of the DataFrame.
12.Stop the program.

3.Source Code

import pandas as pd
import numpy as np
# Load Data
data = {
    "Team": ["CSK", "MI", "RCB", "KKR", "CSK"],
    "Runs": [180, np.nan, 200, 175, 190],
    "Wickets": [5, 7, None, 6, 8]
}
df = pd.DataFrame(data)
print("Original Data:\n", df)
# Check Missing Values
print("\nMissing Values:\n", df.isna().sum())
# Clean Data
df["Runs"] = df["Runs"].fillna(df["Runs"].mean())
df["Wickets"] = df["Wickets"].fillna(df["Wickets"].mean())
print("\nAfter Cleaning\n", df)
# Explore Data
print("\nFirst 5 Rows:\n", df.head())
print("\nInfo:")
df.info()
print("\nStatistical Summary\n", df.describe())
print("\nShape (rows, columns):", df.shape)

