1.Aim

Write a program to implement various types of visualization in python.

2.Algorithm

1.Start the program
2.Import Pandas and Matplotlib libraries.
3.Create a sample dataset containing Month and Sales.
4.Create a line plot to represent monthly sales.
5.Create a bar plot to compare monthly sales.
6.Create a scatter plot to display the relationship between month and sales.
7.Create a histogram to show sales distribution.
8.Create a pie chart to represent sales share.
9.Display all the visualizations.
10.Stop the program

3.Source Code

import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

# Sample Data
df = pd.DataFrame({
    "Month": ["Jan", "Feb", "Mar", "Apr"],
    "Sales": [200, 250, 300, 290]
})

# Line Plot
plt.figure()
plt.plot(df["Month"], df["Sales"])
plt.title("Line Plot - Monthly Sales")
plt.xlabel("Month")
plt.ylabel("Sales")
plt.show()

# Bar Plot
plt.figure()
plt.bar(df["Month"], df["Sales"])
plt.title("Bar Plot - Monthly Sales")
plt.xlabel("Month")
plt.ylabel("Sales")
plt.show()

# Scatter Plot
plt.figure()
plt.scatter(df["Month"], df["Sales"])
plt.title("Scatter Plot - Monthly Sales")
plt.xlabel("Month")
plt.ylabel("Sales")
plt.show()

# Histogram
plt.figure()
plt.hist(df["Sales"])
plt.title("Histogram - Sales Distribution")
plt.xlabel("Sales")
plt.ylabel("Frequency")
plt.show()

# Pie Chart
plt.figure()
plt.pie(df["Sales"], labels=df["Month"],
        autopct="%1.1f%%")
plt.title("Pie Chart - Sales Share")
plt.show()

